{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Additive Cheon with a seven-instruction worst-case parity key",
  "claims": [
    {
      "statement": "For the protected BLS12-381 G1 powers-of-tau target, for every 2^20 <= n < r, the complete cold classical algorithm supplied in proof.md and source-proof.md recovers the scalar s with success probability at least 0.39 over uniform full-production challenges and fresh coins under the explicitly retained H1-H5 heuristics. Its total work W(n)=W(2^20) is at most 2^116.320067 in the protected C=2000 instruction-equivalent units. The scored exact rational is 116320067/1000000. All preprocessing, failures, transfers, lookup, verification and output are included; preprocessing is below 2^115.3235 units and peak memory below 2^121.5854 bytes, with zero advice. Only A_1 and A_(2^20) are read. The sole change to the fully supplied source algorithm is a value-preserving branch-local parity-key block with a deterministic maximum of seven instructions instead of ten. No distribution of branch outcomes is assumed. The inherited side-output kernel price 1054 becomes the analytic upper price 1051; pair and root bookkeeping become 53 and 50 respectively. K=0.4952, f=0.98, all caps and success assumptions remain unchanged. The recomputed conditional success floor exceeds 0.390050. The claim is exploratory and conditional on the supplied production hypotheses, not a full-size execution or an unconditional cryptanalytic theorem.",
      "score": {
        "numerator": "116320067",
        "denominator": "1000000"
      },
